+"""Metadata seeding for all CRM business modules.
+
+Split out of :mod:`seed` because the field definitions run long. Called from
+``seed()`` after the admin user exists (default views need a ``created_by``).
+
+Everything here is idempotent:
+  * ``module_fields`` uses ``(module_id, field_name)`` ``ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE``
+    so re-seeding overwrites label / type / sort_order / options while
+    preserving admin-owned ``field_config`` edits (see ``_upsert_module_field``).
+  * ``module_views`` is looked-up-by-``(module_id, name)`` then either updated
+    in place or inserted; ``module_view_fields`` is replaced atomically via
+    :class:`ModuleViewFieldsDb.set_view_fields` so column order changes stick.
+
+The kacrm-era ``collection_fields`` table is gone as of alembic 0082 —
+``module_fields`` is the sole metadata source, with frontend-widget hints
+folded into its ``field_config`` JSON.
+"""
