+# Patch20 gateway/platform port to v0.21.6
+
+Source: committed hermes-patches/20-gateway-cloud-hooks.patch. All 128 owned rejected hunks are accounted for below. Hunk IDs are old-side start lines from the reject headers. No tests, agent files, parent scripts or patches were edited by this port worker.
+
+## Live-path decisions
+
+- API cloud mixin owns model/provider override, peer channel push and reload routes. OpenAI and durable-run handlers bind origin/user/session/surface/scope ContextVars; counted worker submission copies the context while retaining native shutdown accounting.
+- Reload builds a scratch adapter map, publishes before disconnecting, preserves old adapters on total connect failure, retains primary pending credential/listener claims, and serializes with native profile reconciliation.
+- Profile resolution fails closed in multiplex mode while preserving upstream pinned runtime identities. Document extraction and media IO run off the event loop.
+- Email owns a bounded context-copying IO executor. Header preauthorization, pinned authentication verification and TLS probes remain native. Empty-whitelist cold inbound retains customer mode; owner/list identity grants and explicit or approved pairing retain authenticated-sender checks. Scoped cloud interaction taps run on inbound/outbound.
+- Feishu retains native approval authorization, delete-message support, lazy SDK imports and websocket thread dispatch. Cloud changes add table fencing, QR flow and an owned websocket executor that preserves upstream copied context.
+- Reasoning callbacks feed an opt-in bounded preview that avoids native/draft prefix mutation and retracts contentless previews. Native final-text reconciliation stays intact. Chat SSE retains native reasoning deltas and adds cloud reasoning/turn-metadata events.
