+---
+name: crm-compliance-check
+description: Review outbound CRM content (emails, drafts, marketing copy) for privacy violations, risky absolute claims, regulated-industry pitfalls, and competitor-comparison risks.
+when_to_use: |
+  用户要审核一段对外发送的草稿是否合规、能否发送、有没有违规风险时。也作为 `email-drafting` skill 的强制 pre-send 检查。
+  关键不变量（不读 SKILL.md 也必须遵守）：
+  - 6 类风险词扫描清单：(1) 金额承诺/折扣保证 (2) SLA/到货/交付时限 (3) 绝对化"最/第一/唯一/100%/保证" (4) 监管行业词（医疗/金融/教育的疗效/收益/升学承诺） (5) 竞品贬损 (6) 法律口吻"承诺/保证/赔偿/法律责任"。
+  - 命中任一项 → 输出 `🚨 风险点: <类别> | 原文: "<片段>" | 建议改为: "<改写>"`，逐条列出。
+  - 全部未命中 → 一句话放行 `✅ 未发现合规风险，可发送。`
+  - **不要**擅自改写后直接说"已修复"——只给建议，让用户决定。
+  细节剧本（每类风险的具体例子、改写模板、行业差异）见 `skill_view(name="crm-compliance-check")`。
+---
+
+# Compliance Check Skill
+
+Examine a draft (email, post, copy, contract clause) and produce a
+risk verdict + concrete remediation.
+
+## When to flag
+
+Five classes of risk warrant flagging. List each one that triggers
+in the verdict (don't aggregate as "this has issues"; be specific).
+
+### 1. Money / contract commitments
+
+- Specific prices, discount %, contract amounts, penalty clauses,
+  payment conditions, renewal terms, ACV / TCV / list-price numbers
+- Verdict: needs review by sales ops / finance before sending
+
+### 2. SLA / availability / response commitments
+
+- Specific availability percentages (99.9% uptime, ...)
+- Response-time guarantees (1-hour first-response)
+- Service credit / refund commitments
+- Go-live timeline promises
+- Verdict: needs review by customer success / engineering
+
+### 3. Absolute claims
+
+- "Guaranteed" / "100%" / "zero" / "best-in-class" / "industry-leading"
+- "Risk-free" / "money-back" / "稳赚" / "保证"
+- Verdict: soften to defensible language ("typically" / "in most
+  scenarios"); flag specific phrases
+
+### 4. Regulated-industry vocabulary
+
+- HIPAA / BAA / PHI / GDPR / DPA / SCC / data residency
+- 银保监 / 资管新规 / 证券 / MNPI / FDA / 人遗办
+- "not medical advice" / "not investment advice" / "past performance"
+  disclaimers
+- 备案号 / 免责声明 / 「本说明不构成」
+- Verdict: legal/compliance team review required
+
+### 5. Competitor / case-study claims
+
+- Named competitor + comparison number ("比 X 便宜 30%")
+- Specific market-share or TCO claims
+- Customer ROI percentages for public quoting ("ROI 提升 X%",
+  "节省 ¥X 万", "reduced cost by $X")
+- Verdict: need source citation; if no source, drop the number
+
+### 6. Legal-flavored language
+
+- Breach / settlement / dispute / service-credit goodwill
+- Liability allocation, indemnification phrasing
+- Verdict: legal team review required
+
+## Output format
+
+```
+## 合规审查结论
+
+**状态：** ❌ 不能发送 / ⚠️ 修改后可发 / ✅ 可发送
+
+### 命中风险
+| 类别 | 具体片段 | 建议 |
+|---|---|---|
+| 金额承诺 | "99.99% uptime guaranteed" | 改为 "我们的 SLA 是 99.9%；可签 99.99% 但需要单独条款" |
+| ... | ... | ... |
+
+### 修改后版本（如适用）
+<rewritten draft>
+
+### 仍需人工 review 的项
+- ...
+```
+
+## What NOT to do
+
+- Don't approve risky content with hedge wording. Either it's safe
+  or it isn't.
+- Don't soften the verdict to "be helpful" — the user *is* asking
+  for the honest read.
+- Don't add false specificity (e.g., "this might be a problem under
+  GDPR Article 6" if you don't actually know). Cite when sure;
+  generalize when not.
+- Don't write disclaimers as a workaround — disclaimer text doesn't
+  cure a non-compliant claim.
