+# CRM Schema Quirks
+
+Cheat sheet for code/queries that touch the CRM tables directly. The
+canonical interface is the CRM tools (``crm_search`` / ``crm_get`` /
+``crm_write``) — these notes are for the **rare** case you need raw
+SQL (debug, projections, custom scanners).
+
+## potentials table
+- PK: `potentials_id` (not `id`)
+- No `stage` column — use `milestone` instead (values include:
+  `initial_contact`, `needs_analysis`, `proposal_sent`, `negotiation`,
+  ... — read picklist via `crm_get_schema` for the full current set)
+- `deleted` is BOOLEAN, not integer — always use `WHERE deleted = false`
+- `amount` is numeric/integer (may be null)
+- Expected close date column is `closingdate` (no underscore), not
+  `closing_date` — a common write-side trap
+
+## tasks table
+- PK: `tasks_id` (not `id`)
+- No `subject` column — use `tasks_name` instead
+- `due_at` is timestamptz (not `due_date`)
+- `status`: `'open'` | `'completed'` | etc.
+- `related_module` + `related_record_id` link to CRM records (may be null)
+- `deleted` is BOOLEAN
+
+## leads table
+- PK: `leads_id` (not `id`)
+- `contact` = contact person name (may be null)
+- `mobile`, `email` — direct contact fields (may be null)
+- `source` — picklist; query schema for current values
+- `convertedstatus` — picklist; `convertedby` / `converteddate` —
+  audit columns populated by the `lead.convert` gateway executor
+- `deleted` is BOOLEAN
+- Days-since: `(CURRENT_DATE - created_at::date)` (cast required for
+  date arithmetic)
+
+## accounts table
+- PK: `accounts_id` (not `id`)
+- `mobile` exists; **no `phone` column** — that's a common write-side
+  trap (the lead-convert executor explicitly skips `phone` for
+  accounts)
+- `leads_id` (BIGINT) — set by the `lead.convert` executor, points
+  back to the source lead
+- `deleted` is BOOLEAN
+- Projection-managed columns (set by `contact_stats` over interactions,
+  not user-editable): `latest_contact_date`, `next_contact_date`,
+  `contact_count`, `deal_count`, `deal_amount`
+
+## interactions table
+- PK: `id` (standard uuid, no `_id` suffix)
+- **No `related_module` / `related_record_id` columns** — interactions
+  are NOT linked to CRM records by foreign keys
+- Instead, use `subjects` (JSONB array of `{"module": "...", "id": ...}`)
+  for record linkage, plus `kind` / `source` / `occurred_at`
+- `source` values include: `'manual'` (SPA手工登记), `'channel:feishu'`,
+  `'channel:wechat'`, `'agent:<profile>:<agent_name>'`
+- `actors` = JSONB array: `[{"id": 1, "type": "user"}, {"type": "agent",
+  "name": "hermes", ...}]`
+- `content` = JSONB (free-form per `kind`); for `kind='contact_log'`:
+  `{"summary": "...", "body": "...", "channel": "phone|wechat|..."}`
+- For "past CRM-related context" across sessions: prefer
+  `session_search` tool over raw SQL on interactions
+
+## gateway_actions table
+- PK: `id` (standard uuid)
+- `kind` examples: `'coach.proposal'`, `'crm.write'`, `'task.create'`,
+  `'memory.write'`, `'lead.convert'`
+- `target` = JSONB `{"id": <int>, "module": "leads|potentials|tasks|accounts|..."}`
+- `params` = JSONB — **severity lives HERE** as `params->>'severity'`,
+  NOT as a top-level column
+- `state` = `'pending_approval'` | `'approved'` | `'executed'` |
+  `'rejected'` | `'blocked'` | `'reverted'` | `'conflict'`
+- `created_at` is timestamptz
+- For coach.proposal cards: `params.action.type` ∈
+  `{'draft_message','task_create'}`, `params.action.draft` is the
+  copy-to-clipboard text
+
+## Correct SQL patterns
+
+```sql
+-- Boolean filter (NOT integer)
+WHERE p.deleted = false
+
+-- Days since date (requires cast)
+(CURRENT_DATE - p.updated_at::date) AS days_since_update
+
+-- Severity inside JSONB params (gateway_actions)
+params->>'severity' AS severity
+
+-- Target JSONB (gateway_actions)
+target->>'id'      AS target_id
+target->>'module'  AS target_module
+
+-- interactions ↔ CRM record join
+WHERE subjects @> '[{"module":"accounts","id":42}]'::jsonb
+```
+
+## What `session_search` covers that SQL doesn't
+
+The `sessions` table (via the `session_search` tool) stores full
+conversation history indexed by time and keyword. Use it for:
+
+- Past coach proposal outcomes (executed vs dismissed, by signal type)
+- User's stated preferences and corrections
+- Context on leads/potentials that no longer exist in DB
+- Anything that lives in conversation prose rather than columns
