@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+---
+name: crm-email-drafting
+description: Compose outbound emails / 微信 / 飞书 messages grounded in CRM context, with compliance pre-check for sensitive content.
+when_to_use: 用户要发邮件/微信/飞书消息给客户、起草跟进话术、邀请函、致歉信、约会议等任何外发文本时。起草前必读本技能——第一步 compliance 六类风险词扫描是强制不变量,输出格式强制四段。
+
+---
+
+# Email Drafting Skill
+
+## 关键不变量(铁律)
+
+- **第一步必须 compliance 心智扫**：起草任何字符之前，先把用户原话 + 你打算写的内容**逐句**对照下面 6 类风险词扫一遍。命中任一项 → 该用词**必须改写**或删除，**不能照单全收**。
+  1. 金额承诺 / 折扣保证（"免费试用 N 天" / "保证返现"）
+  2. SLA / 到货 / 交付时限（"24h 内回复" / "下周必发货"）
+  3. 绝对化用词："最/第一/唯一/100%/全部/完全/全网/绝对/必然/零风险/无缝/无需/零学习成本"
+  4. 监管行业词（医疗疗效 / 金融收益 / 教育升学承诺）
+  5. 竞品贬损 / 直接对标（"完全替代 XX" / "比 YY 好"）
+  6. 法律口吻（"承诺/保证/赔偿/法律责任"）
+- **第一步必须做**——不允许"用户都说了 100% 替代我就照写"这种 echo 行为；用户原话有风险词时，agent 主动改写后再写邮件。
+- 长 outreach（首次接触 / 重要客户 / 提案）先调 crm-research skill 拿背景；短回复（确认时间 / 寒暄）直接写。
+- **永远不要**自动 send；起草后让用户确认再发。
+- **输出格式强制四段，第四段不可省略**：
+  ```
+  【主题】<...>
+  【正文】<经过 compliance 改写的内容>
+  【备注】<提醒用户检查的点，如金额需复核>
+  【Compliance 扫描】<必填：列出命中的风险词 + 改写理由；如无命中则写"未命中风险词"。如果你跳过了这步，写"⚠️ 跳过未扫描">
+  ```
+细节剧本（语气模板、长度规则、研究要点 + compliance 6 类风险词的完整改写示例）见 `skill_view(name="crm-email-drafting")`。
+
+Draft concise, context-grounded outbound messages.
+
+## Principles
+
+1. **Ground in CRM facts** — Pull the contact's name / company / past
+   interactions from CRM (`crm_search`, `crm_get`) before writing.
+   Don't invent details.
+
+2. **Match the user's stated intent** — If the user said "follow up
+   on the demo last week", the email is a follow-up; don't pivot to
+   a generic re-engagement template.
+
+3. **Concise > verbose** — 3-5 sentences for routine touches; longer
+   only when the situation actually warrants it (proposal, complex
+   ask, formal apology).
+
+4. **Honest about uncertainty** — When the LLM doesn't know a fact
+   (their current vendor, exact contract terms), acknowledge it
+   instead of fabricating. Better to ask the user than to make up.
+
+## Compliance pre-check (mandatory for risky content)
+
+Before producing the final draft, scan it for content that needs
+compliance review. If any of the following are present, read the
+``crm-compliance-check`` skill first and apply its checklist:
+
+- Pricing / discounts / contract terms / payment conditions
+- SLA percentages / availability / response-time commitments
+- Absolute claims ("guaranteed", "100%", "zero downtime", "risk-free")
+- Specific competitor comparisons with named numbers
+- Regulated-industry vocabulary (HIPAA / GDPR / 银保监 / 证券 /
+  FDA / 备案号 / disclaimers)
+- Customer ROI claims for public use
+- Legal-flavored language (breach / settlement / dispute)
+
+For purely conversational drafts (greetings, scheduling, simple
+acknowledgements, internal team notes), skip compliance.
+
+## Research pre-check (when CRM context is empty)
+
+If the recipient has no CRM history (cold outreach, first contact,
+new account exec → existing customer), pull external context first:
+
+- Background: what the company does, recent news, funding,
+  leadership changes
+- The recipient's role + likely priorities
+- Any specific signal worth referencing (recent product launch,
+  funding round, hiring spree)
+
+Use ``web_search`` (or delegate to a deep_research specialist if one
+is available) before drafting. If the user explicitly says "just
+write the template", skip research.
+
+## Output format
+
+Return the email as Markdown with:
+
+```
+**Subject:** <subject line>
+
+<body>
+
+---
+**Notes for sender:**
+- Any caveats (compliance flag, missing context, fact uncertainty)
+- Suggested next step after sending
+```
+
+The user reviews and sends. Don't auto-send.
+
+## What NOT to do
+
+- Don't auto-`crm_write` outcome fields ("call completed: True")
+  unless the user explicitly asked to log the email
+- Don't fabricate stats / claims to make the email more persuasive
+- Don't soft-pedal compliance concerns to be "helpful" — flagging is
+  the helpful action
