+# Wikipedia REST API for Company/Person Research
+
+## Why use it
+
+- No API key required
+- No bot detection (unlike Google/DuckDuckGo/Bloomberg)
+- Structured JSON output with extract, infobox data, categories
+- Reliable for established companies and notable individuals
+
+## Endpoints
+
+### Summary (1-paragraph intro + metadata)
+
+```
+GET https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/summary/<EntityName>
+```
+
+Returns JSON with: `extract`, `extract_html`, `url`, `thumbnail`, `pageid`, `titles`, `lang`, `description`.
+
+Good for a quick overview. Example fields available for ByteDance:
+- `extract`: "ByteDance is a Chinese internet technology company..."
+- Page provides links to the full article
+
+### Full HTML (for infobox extraction)
+
+```
+GET https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/html/<EntityName>
+```
+
+Returns full article HTML. Infobox data (revenue, CEO, founded, employees, key people, products) can be extracted by parsing `<table class="infobox">` rows.
+
+## Python usage pattern
+
+```python
+import urllib.request, json
+
+url = "https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/summary/ByteDance"
+req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64)"})
+resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10)
+data = json.loads(resp.read())
+print(data.get("extract", ""))
+```
+
+## Entity name encoding
+
+- Use the exact English article title (case-sensitive)
+- Spaces are fine in URL (browser handles encoding)
+- For Chinese entities: use English name if available (e.g. "ByteDance" not "字节跳动")
+- If the first name fails, try variants: "TikTok" → "ByteDance"
+
+## Infobox extraction (from HTML endpoint)
+
+```python
+import re, urllib.request
+
+url = "https://en.wikipedia.org/api/rest_v1/page/html/ByteDance"
+req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0"})
+resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15)
+html = resp.read().decode("utf-8")
+
+# Find the infobox table
+infobox_area = re.search(r'infobox[^>]*>(.*?)</table', html, re.DOTALL)
+if infobox_area:
+    rows = re.findall(r'<tr[^>]*>(.*?)</tr>', infobox_area.group(1), re.DOTALL)
+    for row in rows:
+        headers = re.findall(r'<th[^>]*>(.*?)</th>', row, re.DOTALL)
+        cells = re.findall(r'<td[^>]*>(.*?)</td>', row, re.DOTALL)
+        if headers and cells:
+            h = re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', '', headers[0]).strip()
+            c = re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', '', cells[0]).strip()
+            if h and c:
+                print(f"{h}: {c}")
+```
+
+## Limitations
+
+- Only covers Wikipedia-notable entities (public companies, well-known people)
+- Not real-time — Wikipedia may lag months behind on funding/valuation changes
+- Some infobox data is embedded in `<style>` blocks or complex HTML rendering (e.g. native_name)
+- For private companies or startups below Wikipedia notability threshold, try Crunchbase, company website, or regulatory filings instead
